  by: agent  # fb96
  actor: jgstern_agent  # fb96
  clock: 2  # fb96
  nonce: fb96  # fb96
  message: "Bears on this item (from WI-gokop-nudub-zunal-zibij-fuvad-libot-bituk-visid, branch jgstern-agent/feat/gokop-scala-inferred-receivers, not yet integrated). Scala now READS the base return-type registry, which already merges load_library_signatures(\"scala\") after the analysed rows (base.py step 4c). The typer looks a static owner up as <Owner>.<member> (a capitalised receiver no binder takes, not an implicitly-imported name), so Runtime.getRuntime().exec(..) becomes typed as soon as a library_signatures/scala.yaml (or the scala loader reusing java.yaml rows) carries Runtime.getRuntime -> java.lang.Runtime. There is still no scala.yaml in the tree; that row file is what is left of the scala half of this item. Not tested here: no scala.yaml exists to test with."  # fb96
- op: discuss  # 0f39
  at: '2026-10-04T08:27:00Z'  # 0f39
  by: agent  # 0f39
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 0f39
  clock: 3  # 0f39
  nonce: 0f39  # 0f39
  message: "WORK DONE 2026-10-04 (agent, concurrent run 10032026). Branch jgstern-agent/fix/jubim (local, not pushed), commit a0aedb8475 on origin/dev 385ec63be1.\n\nPremise re-verified before the change: on fxkt / fxsc, exec emitted kotlin:external:0-0:exec and scala:external:0-0:exec; verify-claims on a secret-into-exec fixture gave inconclusive for both the taint claim and a subprocess must_not_exist claim, in both languages.\n\nMechanism: library_signatures.ROW_PARENTS = {kotlin: java, scala: java}, so kotlin and scala read java.yaml's rows (user channel included) with no copied rows. Kotlin: _library_call_type folds a call chain over the rows (root = typed local, import/java.lang type, inline JDK path, or constructor) for the chained receiver and for a local bound to a chain. Scala: _ScalaReceiverTyper._member asks a library owner under its qualified path first; a project type has no library path, so analysed rows still win.\n\nBehavioral evidence (python -m hypergumbo_core verify-claims, fresh caches, before = origin/dev, after = branch): kotlin chained/bound and scala chained/bound, secret -> Runtime.getRuntime().exec: SECRET-NOT-EXEC inconclusive -> violated, NO-SUBPROCESS inconclusive -> violated. Control (secret read in one function, exec(\"ls\") in another): SECRET-NOT-EXEC stays inconclusive (not violated), NO-SUBPROCESS -> violated; same verdicts java gives on the java twin. Kotlin's flow carries confidence approximate where java's carries precise (pre-existing DDG coverage difference, not touched).\n\nTests: red run 25 failed / 25 passed (new tests vs origin/dev source); targeted smart-test on the branch 11511 passed, scoped coverage 100% (2 failures were my wrong boundary name db_query, corrected to db_read; re-run 216 passed). Mutations: disabling the project-type check (kotlin + scala) and letting an unknown link keep its owner (kotlin) turned exactly the 3 controls red, positives green.\n\nMeasured by call site (every calls edge dumped, diffed on (src, line, callee)): detekt 1, okhttp 1, sbt 29, gatling 0 sites change slot external -> JDK type; no site added or lost. Of the changed sites, newly classified: 5 host_info_read + 1 fs_write (sbt), no subprocess/env finding in these four repos (they contain no kotlin/scala Runtime.exec). On the scala3/spark directories holding every Runtime.exec in the corpus's kotlin/scala (grep): 7 of 7 exec sites now classify java.lang.Runtime.exec subprocess, 0 before; 18 new typed edges, all read against source and correct. Not measured: whole scala3 / spark (167 / 302 MB).\n\nResidual filed: WI-bojud-sator-tutad-sohut-fojis-lukuv-hogif-kamuz (scala parameterless calls and kotlin synthetic getters emit no calls edge -- why gatling's Runtime.getRuntime.availableProcessors gained nothing)."  # 0f39
